{"id": "SGU_Episode_489", "title": "SGU Episode 489", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 489 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 489", "date": "November 22 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 11, "day": 22, "rogues": ["Rebecca Watson", "Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigmund_Freud", "quote": "\n The voice of reason is small, but very persistent. \n", "quotee": "\n Sigmund Freud  memorial\n", "quotee_title": "", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-489", "episode_number": 489}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Down under tour\nYou're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "November 22, 1963: JFK Assassination http://www.jfklibrary.org/JFK/JFK-in-History/November-22-1963-Death-of-the-President.aspx", "title": "This Day in Skepticism", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:01:03", "hour": 0, "minute": "1", "second": "03", "links": ["http://www.jfklibrary.org/JFK/JFK-in-History/November-22-1963-Death-of-the-President.aspx"], "title": "This Day in Skepticism"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "IMDB.com: Interstellar\n(Commercial at 40:17)\n", "title": "Special", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:07:00", "hour": 0, "minute": "7", "second": "00", "links": ["http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0816692/"], "title": "Special"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 3, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 4, "text": "http://www.cnn.com/2014/11/12/world/comet-landing-countdown/index.html", "title": "Landing on a Comet", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:41:47", "hour": 0, "minute": "41", "second": "47", "links": ["http://www.cnn.com/2014/11/12/world/comet-landing-countdown/index.html"], "title": "Landing on a Comet"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 5, "text": "http://theness.com/neurologicablog/index.php/feeling-of-presence-induced-in-the-lab/", "title": "Feeling of Presence", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:44:46", "hour": 0, "minute": "44", "second": "46", "links": ["http://theness.com/neurologicablog/index.php/feeling-of-presence-induced-in-the-lab/"], "title": "Feeling of Presence"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 6, "text": "http://www.sci-news.com/physics/science-techni-higgs-discovery-higgs-boson-02266.html", "title": "Doubting the Higgs", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:51:04", "hour": 0, "minute": "51", "second": "04", "links": ["http://www.sci-news.com/physics/science-techni-higgs-discovery-higgs-boson-02266.html"], "title": "Doubting the Higgs"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "http://www.theskepticsguide.org/ food-babe-misinformation-on-travel", "title": "Food Babe Nonsense", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:56:03", "hour": 0, "minute": "56", "second": "03", "links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org/"], "title": "Food Babe Nonsense"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 8, "text": "Answer to last week: Penguins", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:06:26", "hour": "1", "minute": "06", "second": "26", "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 9, "text": "Year End Wrap Up\n(Commercial at 1:08:24)\n", "title": "Announcement", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:07:48", "hour": "1", "minute": "07", "second": "48", "title": "Announcement"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 10, "text": "Item #1: New research indicates that a stimulant drug, modafinil, enhances cognitive performance for those at the low end of the spectrum, but impairs performance for healthy individuals.\nItem #2: The USDA has approved a new genetically modified potato that has 40% of the calories of existing cultivars typically used for chips and fries.\nItem #3: New research in mice finds an association between the type of bacteria found in the gut and the presence of mental behaviors suggestive of anxiety, depression, and autism.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:10:01", "hour": "1", "minute": "10", "second": "01", "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:23:15", "hour": "1", "minute": "23", "second": "15", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 12, "text": "\u201cThe voice of reason is small, but very persistent.\u201d - Sigmund Freud memorial", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}, {"id": 13, "text": "The Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information on this and other episodes, please visit our website at theskepticsguide.org, where you will find the show notes as well as links to our blogs, videos, online forum, and other content. You can send us feedback or questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. Also, please consider supporting the SGU by visiting the store page on our website, where you will find merchandise, premium content, and subscription information. Our listeners are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/shop"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 14, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}